# Flamenco Rhythm: the 12-Beat Cycle (repertoire plan: st-solea-compas). An original study in
# the rhythm of solea: a cycle of 12 counts with accents on 3, 6, 8, 10 and 12, written as four
# bars of 3/4 (counts 1-3, 4-6, 7-9, 10-12). E (022100) is home; F (xx3211) on counts 7-9 pulls
# back down to E on count 10, where every cycle comes to rest.
# Your right hand: each accented count is a four-finger rasgueado, four sixteenth-note
# downstrokes (little, ring, middle, index), the first one strong (written as the full chord with
# an accent mark); every other count is one soft downstroke with the side of the thumb.
# Four cycles of compas (bars 1-16), then a closing falseta of two cycles (bars 17-24): a short
# melody in E Phrygian (E F G A B C D), every note a thumb rest stroke, accents still on 3, 6, 8,
# 10 and 12, closing on an E chord on count 10.
# The key signature is that of A minor: E Phrygian uses the same notes, centred on E.
title: Flamenco Rhythm: the 12-Beat Cycle
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original study in the rhythm of solea
licence: Original study for Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 7
tags: flamenco, solea, compas, rasgueado, phrygian, accents, 12 beats
tempo: 108
time: 3/4
key: Am

track: Your part
role: rhythm
